Maybe a plate of sashimi?

253
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:40,405
I'll make one hell of a
meal out of your stand.

254
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,191
Don't play games with me.

255
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:45,297
You're trying to sound tough,
but I know the truth, boy.

256
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:49,317
The real terror of all this is
starting to sink into your thick skull.

257
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:51,317
I can even tell what you're thinking.

258
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,300
How long can he stay underwater?

259
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:57,897
I can probably last about two minutes,
but can he last longer than me?

260
00:15:57,980 --> 00:15:59,156
Am I right, brother?

261
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,940
Let me answer you.

262
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:06,240
My lung capacity is three
times that of a normal human's.

263
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,840
See, for years I've been training.

264
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:12,498
Six minutes and 12 seconds
is my best submerged time.

265
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:16,191
You must be dizzy just hearing
that number, right, brother?

266
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,550
And...

267
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:23,960
Dark Blue Moon's fins are cutters that
move faster than a ship's propeller,

268
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,300
far sharper too.

269
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,880
Before you get overconfident again,

270
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:30,957
you might want to take a
good hard look at your stand.

271
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,497
Seems Dark Blue Moon's
barnacles have taken

272
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,992
a liking to absorbing your stand's power.

273
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:41,060
How does it feel to have your life energy
slowly draining away from your body?

274
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:46,157
Trying to run away by swimming back up?

275
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,260
Take a good look around you!

276
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:54,584
Haven't you realized, brother, Dark Blue
Moon has created an underwater whirlpool?

277
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:59,060
There's no way you can possibly
escape! That's right! Swim faster!

278
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:02,997
You'll just make it harder to breathe
while your power keeps draining!

279
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:08,020
But it's a little too early to kill a
stupid, smart-ass punk like you just yet!

280
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:10,200
It's been too long!

281
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,897
He's still not coming up!

282
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,260
A giant whirlpool!

283
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,991
It must have him trapped!

284
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:17,900
Where the hell is Jojo?

285
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:19,474
Let's go and save him.

286
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:26,720
These are scales.

287
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:30,060
That guy's stand has
scales as sharp as razors.

288
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:33,197
There are countless scales
swirling in that whirlpool.

289
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:36,537
He wasn't bluffing when he said he
could beat all five of us at once.

290
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:38,780
It's like a watery antlion pit.

291
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:43,089
If we dive in, it's very possible
we'll be sliced to pieces.

292
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:46,340
His scales?

293
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:54,177
I'll take another guess
at what you're thinking.

294
00:17:54,260 --> 00:17:56,780
In a whirlpool, only one spot stays still.

295
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,220
Such mundane logic.

296
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:01,720
It's the eye.

297
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:05,234
If I jump into the center
where he is, I can attack him.

298
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,937
That's what you're thinking, right?

299
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:11,177
If you believe you can hit me
with that punch of yours again,

300
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:13,420
Then come and give it a shot.

301
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,780
Throw your worthless stand at me.

302
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,597
Its power's so drained
it doesn't have a chance.

303
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,580
See if you can manage an attack,

304
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:23,577
one that's even sharper than
these underwater cutters.

305
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:24,940
I'm waiting, brother!

306
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,360
Damn him!

307
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,349
We're completely helpless!

308
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:31,560
It's Jojo!

309
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:35,420
I just saw Jojo in the whirlpool. Buddha!

310
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:37,517
I don't think he's moving down there.

311
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:38,880
So he went limp?

312
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:41,569
He wasn't struggling
against the whirlpool?

313
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:45,040
Oh, well, that might
actually be a good thing.

314
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:49,760
Weren't you gonna turn
me into sashimi boy?

315
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:54,800
You're the one who's gonna be sliced up!

316
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:03,990
Starfinger!

317
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:11,860
Sorry, did I interrupt you?

318
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:13,669
Who's going to be sashimi?

319
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:17,760
What's that?

320
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:19,120
I can't hear you.

321
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:21,237
You're going to have to speak up.

322
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:22,320
We're underwater.

323
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:24,641
But your power was being drained.

324
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:27,840
You let yourself go live
on purpose, didn't you?

325
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:30,337
You concentrated your
power in your fingers.

326
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,773
That's what you were thinking all along.

327
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,240
Not even close.

328
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:40,380
The only thing on my mind
is how gross it'll be

329
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:44,037
when I kick your stupid ass and
you piss yourself under water.

330
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,002
And that's all.

331
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,800
Bye, pups.

332
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,290
Jojo!

333
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,980
That's my grandson for ya.

334
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,317
Well done, Jotaro.

335
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,380
Hurry and come-a-her!

336
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:14,240
That captain planted some
bombs after all! Damn it!

337
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:17,200
Send out a distress call!

338
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:53,101
Here, you should have some water.

339
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:54,737
We've sent out distress calls,

340
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:58,173
so someone should be here with
a rescue ship soon enough.

341
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,677
Okay, just what the hell is going on here?

342
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,172
I don't get any of this.

343
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:04,300
Who are you guys?

344
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,940
Just think of us as fellow travelers.

345
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:10,114
You're on a journey to see your father,

346
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:12,600
while I'm on one for my daughter.

347
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:21,152
Hey, that's the only fresh water we have.

348
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:22,417
So don't spit it out.

349
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,330
We need it.

350
00:21:23,413 --> 00:21:24,243
No, no.

351
00:21:24,326 --> 00:21:25,156
No!

352
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:29,860
Everyone look there! Mm-hmm.

353
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:31,750
Huh?

354
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:57,397
All the old paintings on the tomb.

355
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,437
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

356
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:00,997
If they move too quick!

357
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:04,157
They're falling down like a domino.

358
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:06,797
All the birds are men by the Nile.

359
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,817
They've got their money on a bed.

360
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,437
Called crocodiles.

361
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,417
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

362
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:15,777
Foreign types with a hookah. I say.

363
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:24,640
Walk like an Egyptian.

364
00:22:36,340 --> 00:22:39,397
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

365
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,397
Spin around and they cross the floor.

366
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:43,917
They've got the moves, oh-hey-oh?

367
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,257
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more.

368
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:50,937
All the school kids so sick of books,
they're like the punk and the metal band.

369
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:55,060
When the buzzer rings, they're
walking like an Egyptian.

370
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,798
All the kids in the marketplace say,

371
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:06,540
Walk like an Egyptian.

372
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:17,457
I can't find a single
sign of human life aboard.

373
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:18,917
I feel sticky from the salt water.

374
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,257
This is what it means
to face death, damn ape.

375
00:23:21,340 --> 00:23:22,752
Thinks he's won already.
